(FIL-40: appending adds to the end of an existing file.
 Write N bytes, close, reopen for appending, write M bytes, close,
 reopen for reading: size is N+M throughout, checked on the live open
 handle each time (a property read AFTER Close reports -1, not the true
 value - discovered by hand while building this probe, see the note in
 REPORT-LEAVES-FILES-B.md).
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-40.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   5
   9
   9
 Then with the final check changed to `is not 10` (a deliberately wrong
 expectation), to prove a failing assertion is classified correctly:
   ASSERT FIL-40: expected 10 got 9
 exit code 95.
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called 'the loading bay' at "vf_scratch/files/fil40.txt".
Write "abcde" to 'the loading bay'.
If 'the loading bay's size is not 5 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-40: expected 5 got {'the loading bay's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the loading bay's size.
Close 'the loading bay'.
open a file for appending called 'the loading bay' at "vf_scratch/files/fil40.txt".
Write "wxyz" to 'the loading bay'.
If 'the loading bay's size is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-40: expected 9 got {'the loading bay's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the loading bay's size.
Close 'the loading bay'.
open a file for reading called 'the loading bay' at "vf_scratch/files/fil40.txt".
If 'the loading bay's size is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-40: expected 9 got {'the loading bay's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the loading bay's size.
Close 'the loading bay'.
